@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About CompileCare | Product vision</PageTitle>
<main class="page-shell">
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="section-kicker">ABOUT COMPILECARE</span><h1>Technology that supports<br/><span>the people behind care.</span></h1><p>CompileCare is an India-focused hospital software initiative building a secure, configurable and extensible platform for connected hospital operations—from patient access and outpatient care to the wider hospital journey.</p></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container architecture-panel">
        <div><span class="section-kicker">OUR VISION</span><h2>One coherent hospital platform, delivered with discipline.</h2><p>Hospitals rely on many teams and systems. Our vision is to connect the operational and clinical workflows that matter, reduce repeated data entry and provide a dependable foundation for future capabilities.</p><p>CompileCare is being developed incrementally. The current implementation establishes tenant, identity, facility, patient, appointment, queue, OPD, billing and workforce foundations. Additional hospital modules are planned and will be introduced only with validated workflows and governance.</p></div>
        <div class="architecture-list"><div><span class="arch-number">01</span><div><b>Patient-centred workflows</b><small>Keep the patient journey connected across teams.</small></div></div><div><span class="arch-number">02</span><div><b>Configurable hospital operations</b><small>Reflect each organization's structure and access model.</small></div></div><div><span class="arch-number">03</span><div><b>Security & privacy by design</b><small>Least privilege, scoped access and accountable actions.</small></div></div><div><span class="arch-number">04</span><div><b>Pragmatic modular architecture</b><small>Complete and validate workflows before expanding scope.</small></div></div></div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section section-dark"><div class="container"><span class="section-kicker light">PRODUCT PRINCIPLES</span><h2>Built around the realities of hospital work.</h2><div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle-card"><div class="principle-icon">◎</div><h3>Reduce repetition</h3><p>Connect registration, scheduling, queue and clinical documentation through explicit workflows.</p></article>
        <article class="principle-card"><div class="principle-icon">⬡</div><h3>Respect boundaries</h3><p>Keep tenant, hospital, department and clinical access boundaries enforced by the API.</p></article>
        <article class="principle-card"><div class="principle-icon">⌘</div><h3>Stay modular</h3><p>Keep capabilities maintainable and independently governed without premature microservices.</p></article>
        <article class="principle-card"><div class="principle-icon">↗</div><h3>Plan for interoperability</h3><p>Design explicit contracts for future standards and partner integrations.</p></article>
    </div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container closing-inline"><div><span class="section-kicker">TRANSPARENT DELIVERY</span><h2>Explore the complete platform scope.</h2><p>See which capabilities have an implementation foundation and which remain planned, then review the technologies used across the repositories.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/features">View platform capabilities →</a></div></section>
</main>